# Unfold the phonons of Pnma CaTiO3 (the child: 20 atoms, child/FORCE_SETS of a
# 2x2x2 supercell) onto the Brillouin zone of cubic Pm-3m CaTiO3 (the parent:
# 5 atoms with Ti at the origin, parent/FORCE_SETS of a 2x2x2 supercell). The
# transformation M and the origin shift p are computed from the two POSCARs by
# the symmetry-mode analysis of crystod-group (next command); --parent-dim adds
# the parent bands, the parent levels at the special points and the child
# levels the soft parent modes go into. Writes phonon_unfold.pdf (page 1:
# parent bands | one domain | domain average, and every arm of the stars of
# the path vertices; page 2: the parent irreps) and phonon_unfold.dat.
crystod-phonon --unfold --child-poscar child/62_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3 --child-dim 2 2 2 --parent-poscar parent/221_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3 --parent-dim 2 2 2

