# Another of the 24 equivalent settings (--trans-mat: nine integers, rows,
# child = T @ parent): the long Pnma axis along the parent c. The condensed
# arms are then M (1/2, 1/2, 0) and X (0, 0, 1/2): the M point of the path is
# the in-phase tilt M3+, which folds onto the child Gamma point, and the X
# point of the path folds onto the child U point. The origin shift follows the
# setting (p = W p0 + w with the parent operation of the setting row). The
# setup, path and star-arm blocks of the output are shown.
crystod-phonon --unfold --child-poscar child/62_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3 --child-dim 2 2 2 --parent-poscar parent/221_PPOSCAR_CaTiO3 --parent-dim 2 2 2 --trans-mat 1 1 0  0 0 2  1 -1 0 -o phonon_unfold_c

